x86_64-windows  this case ends in a diamond, and a diamond is refused for this target by the message virtual-base-diamond.notarget sets out: cl gives a class that inherits a virtual base along two paths one vbtable per path, and cxx1 emits one. The rest of the Microsoft virtual-base layout - the vbptr, the table, the constructor's store into it and reading a member through it - **landed on 2026-09-10** and is held by virtual-base-vbtable.cpp. What this case measures - which constructor the most-derived class calls for a virtual base, and with what arguments - is an Itanium question until the second table lands.
